---
import site from "../data/site.json";
import simulation from "../data/hero-media.json";
import media from "../../public/media/evtol-clips.json";
const clips = media.clips;
---

<section id="media-description" class="media-description" aria-labelledby="media-heading">
  <p class="eyebrow">Real-world context and simulation</p>
  <h2 id="media-heading">Video descriptions & sources</h2>
  <section aria-labelledby="context-description-heading">
    <h3 id="context-description-heading">NASA and Joby air-taxi testing</h3>
    <p><a href={site.contextUrl}>{site.contextCredit}</a></p>
    <div id="context-visual-description">
      {site.contextDetails.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
    </div>
    <p class="fine-print">{site.contextLicense}{" "}<a href={site.contextLicenseUrl}>Source and media-use information</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="simulation-description-heading">
    <h3 id="simulation-description-heading">{simulation.title}</h3>
    <div id="simulation-visual-description">
      {simulation.description.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
    </div>
    <p class="fine-print">{simulation.credit}</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="excerpts-heading">
    <h3 id="excerpts-heading">Urban flight excerpts</h3>
    <div id="excerpts-visual-description">
      {clips.map((clip) => <div class="excerpt-credit"><h4>{clip.title}</h4><p>{clip.description}</p></div>)}
      <p>These clips are successive excerpts of the same Flying DNA presentation animation, not separate experiments. They are shown at original speed, without cropping or audio. They do not establish controller identity, wind conditions, quantitative performance, or real-aircraft validation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <p class="fine-print">All videos are silent and include text alternatives. Visible videos can play automatically; native player controls remain available to pause or resume each video. Manual pauses are remembered. Reduced-motion and data-saving preferences suppress automatic playback. The NASA/Joby recording and presentation animation illustrate separate settings.</p>
</section>
